<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Said Musa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Said Musa is a Belizean lawyer and politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-united-party">People's United Party</a> who served as prime minister of Belize from 1998 to 2008. One of the generation of leaders who followed independence in 1981, he alternated in power with the United Democratic Party. His governments were marked by economic liberalisation and later by controversy over public debt, and he lost the 2008 election to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dean-barrow">Dean Barrow</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/said-musa.jpg" alt="Said Musa" width="210" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Debra Gulbas, White House photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Said_Musa_2007.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
